---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import { SITE } from "../../lib/site";
import { localizePath , pick } from "../../i18n/utils";

const lang = (Astro.currentLocale ?? "en") as "en" | "zh";

const slug = "authentication-and-keys";

const C = pick({
  en: {
    heading: "Authentication and SSH keys",
    intro:
      "VVTerm signs in with a password, an SSH key, or an SSH key protected by a passphrase. Here is how each method works and where your credentials are stored.",
    meta: "Documentation",
    title: "Authentication and SSH keys — VVTerm",
    description:
      "Password, SSH key, and SSH key with passphrase authentication in VVTerm, and how credentials are kept in the Apple Keychain rather than synced metadata.",
    schemaDescription:
      "VVTerm authentication methods explained: password, SSH key, and SSH key with passphrase, plus how credentials are stored in the Apple Keychain.",
    bodyHtml: `
  <p>
    Authentication is set per server, so different machines can use different methods. VVTerm supports
    three options, and whichever you choose, the secret itself is stored in the Apple Keychain rather
    than in the server definition that syncs through iCloud.
  </p>

  <h2>Authentication methods</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Password</strong> — you enter the account password for the server. It is the quickest
      way to confirm that a host, port, and username are correct, and a fine choice for machines you
      control. The password is saved to the Keychain so you do not retype it each time.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>SSH key</strong> — you authenticate with a private key instead of a password. The
      matching public key must be present in the server's <code>~/.ssh/authorized_keys</code> file.
      Key-based login is more secure than a password and supports passwordless sign-in.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>SSH key + passphrase</strong> — the same as an SSH key, but the private key is itself
      encrypted with a passphrase. Even if the key is exposed, it cannot be used without the
      passphrase, which adds a layer of protection for sensitive hosts.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Where credentials live</h2>
  <p>
    Passwords, private keys, and passphrases are stored in the <strong>Apple Keychain</strong>. They
    are <strong>not</strong> included in the server metadata that VVTerm syncs through iCloud
    (CloudKit). That means your server list can travel between devices while the secrets stay in the
    secure, system-managed store.
  </p>
  <p>
    Credentials sync between your devices only when <strong>iCloud Keychain</strong> is enabled in iOS
    or macOS settings. With it on, a key or password saved on one device becomes available on the
    others. With it off, credentials stay local to the device they were entered on, and you add them
    again where needed. For the full picture of what syncs and what does not, see <a href="/docs/icloud-sync">iCloud sync and Keychain</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Generating and importing keys</h2>
  <p>
    If you do not already have an SSH key, VVTerm can generate one for you. After generating, copy the
    public key and add it to the server's <code>~/.ssh/authorized_keys</code> file, then select that
    key as the server's authentication method. If you have an existing private key, import it into
    VVTerm and assign it to the server the same way.
  </p>
  <p>
    A public key on the server is what authorizes a private key on your device. You can reuse one key
    pair across many servers by placing the same public key in each server's <code>authorized_keys</code>, or keep separate keys per host for tighter control.
  </p>

  <h2>Verifying the host</h2>
  <p>
    The first time you connect to a server, VVTerm shows the host's key fingerprint. Confirm it
    matches what you expect before accepting, so you can be sure you are connecting to the right
    machine and not an impostor. After you trust a host, later connections proceed without prompting
    unless its key changes.
  </p>

  <h2>Next steps</h2>
  <p>
    With authentication set up, move on to <a href="/docs/sftp-file-browser">the SFTP file browser</a> to manage remote files, or revisit <a href="/docs/adding-a-server">Adding a server</a> to tune the
    connection details.
  </p>
`,
  },
  zh: {
    heading: "认证与 SSH 密钥",
    intro:
      "VVTerm 通过密码、SSH 密钥或受口令保护的 SSH 密钥登录。这里说明每种方式如何工作，以及你的密钥保存在哪里。",
    meta: "文档",
    title: "认证与 SSH 密钥 — VVTerm",
    description:
      "VVTerm 中的密码、SSH 密钥及带口令的 SSH 密钥认证，以及密钥如何保存在 Apple Keychain 而非同步的元数据中。",
    schemaDescription:
      "VVTerm 认证方式解析：密码、SSH 密钥和带口令的 SSH 密钥，以及密钥如何保存在 Apple Keychain 中。",
    bodyHtml: `
  <p>
    认证是按服务器设置的，因此不同机器可以使用不同方式。VVTerm 支持三种选项，无论你选哪一种，密钥本身都保存在 Apple Keychain 中，而非通过 iCloud 同步的服务器定义里。
  </p>

  <h2>认证方式</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>密码</strong> —— 你输入该服务器的账户密码。这是确认主机、端口和用户名是否正确的最快方式，对你掌控的机器是个不错的选择。密码会保存到 Keychain，这样你不必每次重新输入。
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>SSH 密钥</strong> —— 你用私钥而非密码进行认证。对应的公钥必须存在于服务器的 <code>~/.ssh/authorized_keys</code> 文件中。基于密钥的登录比密码更安全，并支持免密码登录。
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>SSH 密钥 + 口令</strong> —— 与 SSH 密钥相同，但私钥本身用一个口令加密。即使密钥被泄露，没有口令也无法使用，这为敏感主机增加了一层保护。
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>密钥保存在哪里</h2>
  <p>
    密码、私钥和口令保存在 <strong>Apple Keychain</strong> 中。它们<strong>不</strong>包含在 VVTerm 通过 iCloud（CloudKit）同步的服务器元数据里。这意味着你的服务器列表可以在设备间流转，而密钥则留在安全的、由系统管理的存储中。
  </p>
  <p>
    只有当 iOS 或 macOS 设置中启用了 <strong>iCloud Keychain</strong> 时，密钥才会在你的设备间同步。开启后，在一台设备上保存的密钥或密码会在其他设备上可用。关闭时，密钥仅留在输入它的设备本地，你需要在需要的地方再次添加。关于哪些会同步、哪些不会的完整说明，参见 <a href="/zh/docs/icloud-sync">iCloud 同步与 Keychain</a>。
  </p>

  <h2>生成与导入密钥</h2>
  <p>
    如果你还没有 SSH 密钥，VVTerm 可以为你生成一个。生成后，复制公钥并把它加入服务器的 <code>~/.ssh/authorized_keys</code> 文件，然后把该密钥选为服务器的认证方式。如果你已有私钥，把它导入 VVTerm 并以同样的方式分配给服务器。
  </p>
  <p>
    服务器上的公钥用于授权你设备上的私钥。你可以把同一个公钥放进每台服务器的 <code>authorized_keys</code>，从而在多台服务器间复用一对密钥；也可以为每台主机保留独立的密钥以获得更严格的控制。
  </p>

  <h2>验证主机</h2>
  <p>
    首次连接某台服务器时，VVTerm 会显示该主机的密钥指纹。在接受前确认它与你预期的一致，这样你就能确定自己连接到的是正确的机器而非冒名者。信任某台主机后，除非它的密钥发生变化，之后的连接会无需提示直接进行。
  </p>

  <h2>后续步骤</h2>
  <p>
    设置好认证后，前往<a href="/zh/docs/sftp-file-browser">SFTP 文件浏览器</a>管理远程文件，或回到<a href="/zh/docs/adding-a-server">添加服务器</a>调整连接细节。
  </p>
`,
  },
}, lang);

const articleSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "TechArticle",
  name: C.heading,
  description: C.schemaDescription,
  url: `${SITE.siteUrl}${localizePath(`/docs/${slug}`, lang)}`,
};
---

<DocsLayout
  kind="docs"
  activeSlug={slug}
  heading={C.heading}
  intro={C.intro}
  meta={C.meta}
  title={C.title}
  description={C.description}
  canonicalPath={`/docs/${slug}`}
  structuredData={[articleSchema]}
>
  <Fragment set:html={C.bodyHtml} />
</DocsLayout>
